<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-substitution-rate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-substitution-rate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Neutral substitution rate equals the mutation rate" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-substitution-rate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "For neutral mutations the long-run rate of molecular substitution equals the mutation rate per generation, independent of population size, which yields a molecular clock." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-substitution-rate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-substitution-rate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "k = 2N\\mu \\cdot \\frac{1}{2N} = \\mu" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-substitution-rate> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: strictly neutral mutations, mutation rate constant per generation, steady state. Formal status: an exact consequence of the neutral fixation probability. Variation in generation time and weak selection on nearly neutral sites cause departures from strict clock-like rates." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-substitution-rate> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Compare the substitution rate at putatively neutral sites (synonymous sites, pseudogenes) across lineages with independently measured per-generation mutation rates from pedigree sequencing." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-substitution-rate> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-substitution-rate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Motoo Kimura (1968) Evolutionary Rate at the Molecular Level" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-substitution-rate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1038/351652a0> .
}
